+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QhJuZZ4TsL8e2HDEHWFu5r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 34 tests pass, build succeeds, and lint is clean.\n\nI found and fixed 6 bugs in the order-processing system:\n\n1. **`events/bus.ts`** — Handlers lived in a module-level `globalHandlers` map shared across every `EventBus` instance, so handlers accumulated across tests (and would across orders in production). Each emit re-fired stale handlers bound to old repositories, causing spurious \"Insufficient stock\" errors. Made the registry a per-instance field.\n\n2. **`billing/service.ts`** — `handleRefund` was registered without `.bind(this)`, so when the `order.refunded` event fired, `this` was undefined and `this.payments` threw. Added the bind (matching the sibling handler).\n\n3. **`billing/calculator.ts`** — Intermediate values (`discountAmount`, `afterDiscount`) were rounded to cents before being used in the next step, accumulating error (130.87 instead of 130.86). Now computes the total at full precision and rounds only the exposed figures.\n\n4. **`orders/repository.ts`** — `update()` built the new record from `{ ...updates }` only, dropping all existing fields. So confirming an order wiped its `items`/`customerId`/etc., breaking cancellation (`order.items.map` on undefined). Now merges `{ ...existing, ...updates, ... }`.\n\n5. **`inventory/service.ts`** — `handleOrderCancelled` early-returned unless the event had `status === 'cancelled'`, but the order service's cancellation event carries no `status` field, so reserved stock was never released. Removed the bogus gate.\n\n6. **`orders/service.ts`** — The refund window check used `>= 30`, rejecting refunds on exactly day 30 which should be allowed. Changed to `> 30`.\n\nThese changes only touch source files; no tests were modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_token